## How to enable/disable FLASH WRP

> - **Device**: STM32F103C6Tx  
> - **Firmware Package**: STM32Cube FW_F1 v1.8.6 (latest)  
> - **Toolchain**: GCC  

When using `HAL_FLASHEx_OBProgram()` to **disable** write protection (WRP) on
specific pages, the resulting Option Byte value is unexpected.

### Code and Log

1. On power-up, all flash pages are **not** write-protected.
2. After enabling WRP on pages 0–31, `WRP0` becomes `0x00`.
3. After **disabling** WRP on pages 0–3, `WRP0` becomes `0xFF`(expected `0x01`)

```c
void print_option_bytes(void)
{
  __IO uint8_t *ob = (__IO uint8_t *)OB_BASE;
  __IO uint8_t *ob_end = (__IO uint8_t *)(OB_BASE + 16);
  printf("ob(%p): ", ob);
  while (ob < ob_end) {
    printf("%02x ", *ob++);
  }
  printf("\b\r\n");
}

void flash_write_wrp(uint8_t wrp_enable, uint32_t wrp)
{
  FLASH_OBProgramInitTypeDef flash_ob;
  flash_ob.OptionType = OPTIONBYTE_WRP;
  flash_ob.WRPState = wrp_enable ? OB_WRPSTATE_ENABLE : OB_WRPSTATE_DISABLE;
  flash_ob.WRPPage = wrp;

  HAL_FLASH_Unlock();
  HAL_FLASH_OB_Unlock();

  HAL_StatusTypeDef result = HAL_FLASHEx_OBProgram(&flash_ob);

  HAL_FLASH_OB_Lock();
  HAL_FLASH_Lock();

  printf("flash_write_wrp ret: %d\r\n", result);
  print_option_bytes();

  HAL_FLASH_OB_Launch();
}

int main(void)
{
  HAL_Init();
  SystemClock_Config();

  MX_GPIO_Init();
  MX_USART2_UART_Init();

  // -- User Code
  printf("system start\r\n");
  print_option_bytes();

  uint8_t ch = 0;
  while (1) {
    if (HAL_UART_Receive(&huart2, &ch, 1, HAL_MAX_DELAY) != HAL_OK) {
      continue;
    }
    printf("\n recv ch: %c(%x)\r\n", ch, ch);
    if (ch == 'w') {
      flash_write_wrp(1, OB_WRP_PAGES0TO31MASK); // protect 0~31
    } else {
      flash_write_wrp(0, OB_WRP_PAGES0TO3); // disable 0~3
    }
  }

  return 0;
}
```

