### Try analysis

The following code is `FLASH_OB_DisableWRP` in STM32F103x6(remove unused code)

1. If `WriteProtectPage` is `0x01`
  - `WriteProtectPage`: will be `0x00 | 0x01 = 0x01`
  - `WRP0_Data`: will be `0x01 & 0xFF = 0x01`
2. After `HAL_FLASHEx_OBErase();`: `OB->WRP0` is `0xFF`,
3. After `OB->WRP0 |= WRP0_Data;`: is `OB->WRP0` is `0xFF | 0x01 = 0xFF`

Is this a bug in the HAL library or a problem caused by incorrect usage on my part?


```c
static HAL_StatusTypeDef FLASH_OB_DisableWRP(uint32_t WriteProtectPage)
{
  HAL_StatusTypeDef status = HAL_OK;
  uint16_t WRP0_Data = 0xFFFF;

  /* Check the parameters */
  assert_param(IS_OB_WRP(WriteProtectPage));

  /* Get current write protected pages and the new pages to be unprotected ******/
  WriteProtectPage = (FLASH_OB_GetWRP() | WriteProtectPage);

  WRP0_Data = (uint16_t)(WriteProtectPage & OB_WRP_PAGES0TO31MASK);

  /* Wait for last operation to be completed */
  status = FLASH_WaitForLastOperation((uint32_t)FLASH_TIMEOUT_VALUE);

  if(status == HAL_OK)
  { 
    /* Clean the error context */
    pFlash.ErrorCode = HAL_FLASH_ERROR_NONE;

    /* To be able to write again option byte, need to perform a option byte erase */
    status = HAL_FLASHEx_OBErase();
    if (status == HAL_OK)  
    {
      SET_BIT(FLASH->CR, FLASH_CR_OPTPG);

      if(WRP0_Data != 0xFFU)
      {
        OB->WRP0 |= WRP0_Data;

        /* Wait for last operation to be completed */
        status = FLASH_WaitForLastOperation((uint32_t)FLASH_TIMEOUT_VALUE);
      }

      /* if the program operation is completed, disable the OPTPG Bit */
      CLEAR_BIT(FLASH->CR, FLASH_CR_OPTPG);
    }
  }
  return status;
}
```

